  "content": {
    "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-upper-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "Solve each of these equations for $0\\leq x<360^{\\circ}$ to the nearest degree.",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-upper-slot-10-upper-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{2}{\\sin x}+3=-1$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=210^{\\circ}$ or $330^{\\circ}$; $\\sin x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, Q3 and Q4.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{2}{\\sin x}+3&=-1\\\\\\frac{2}{\\sin x}&=-4\\\\2&=-4\\sin x\\\\\\sin x&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\A&=\\sin^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\\\A&=30^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nSine is negative in Q3 and Q4.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=180^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ}\\\\x&=210^{\\circ}\\\\x&=360^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\x&=330^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-upper-slot-10-upper-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{3}{2\\cos x}=-\\sqrt{3}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=150^{\\circ}$ or $210^{\\circ}$; $\\cos x=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$, Q2 and Q3.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{3}{2\\cos x}&=-\\sqrt{3}\\\\3&=-2\\sqrt{3}\\cos x\\\\\\cos x&=-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{3}}\\\\\\cos x&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\\\A&=\\cos^{-1}\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\right)\\\\A&=30^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nCosine is negative in Q2 and Q3.\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=180^{\\circ}-30^{\\circ}\\\\x&=150^{\\circ}\\\\x&=180^{\\circ}+30^{\\circ}\\\\x&=210^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      },
      {
        "id": "v2-1ddc9-p55-practice-slot-10-upper-slot-10-upper-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\dfrac{1}{\\tan x}-3=-5$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$x\\approx153^{\\circ}$ or $333^{\\circ}$; $\\tan x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, Q2 and Q4.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{\\tan x}-3&=-5\\\\\\frac{1}{\\tan x}&=-2\\\\1&=-2\\tan x\\\\\\tan x&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\A&=\\tan^{-1}\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\end{align*}$$\nTangent is negative in Q2 and Q4. Using the unrounded value of $A$:\n$$\\begin{align*}x&=180^{\\circ}-A\\\\x&\\approx153^{\\circ}\\\\x&=360^{\\circ}-A\\\\x&\\approx333^{\\circ}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 40
      }
    ]
  },
